--- !u!114 &-6259221703712119993
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a61b9e76000000000000000000000044, type: 3}
  m_Name: ShrineA2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: MissNibiru.Narrative::MissNibiru.Narrative.NarrativeLineNode
  id: shrinea2_line
  editorPosition: {x: 1075, y: 5405}
  character: {fileID: 0}
  emotion: {fileID: 0}
  portraitSide: 0
  text: "You move away from the door quickly, pushing yourself through the room just
    as the door begins to open and footsteps enter the room.\n\nYou can't look back
    now, but you stay a little longer. You breathe slowly, calming yourself down...At
    the edge of your vision you see her drifting towards the middle of the room.
    <i>\"What is this?\"</i> She reaches the figure. You see her eyes widen as she
    looks at him. <color=#a674e8>\"Oh? Is this him?\"</color> You don\u2019t answer
    but turn and look. She circles around him once, her gaze moving over him. <color=#a674e8>\"...he
    doesn\u2019t look <i>that</i> old.\"</color> She focuses her eyes on you, smiles,
    and with that, disappears. A sharp pain hits your head and your vision starts
    to blur.The figure starts speaking. <color=#c1121f>\u201CNyx, eternal goddess
    of the night\u2026\u201D</color>\n\nYou try to focus but... the words slip past
    you... it's so hard to make sense of any of it.\n\n<color=#c1121f>\u201C\u2026younger\u2026\u201D</color>
    You blink. <color=#c1121f>\"...understood, it shall be adjusted.\"</color>\n\nYou
    bring your hands to your temples and scoff under your breath. You barely got
    to hear anything, but the pain is sharp. You need to move."
  importedSegments:
  - text: 'You move away from the door quickly, pushing yourself through the room
      just as the door begins to open and footsteps enter the room.


      You can''t
      look back now, but you stay a little longer. You breathe slowly, calming yourself
      down...'
