--- !u!114 &2725743274395299415
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a61b9e76000000000000000000000044, type: 3}
  m_Name: Serena_Know
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: MissNibiru.Narrative::MissNibiru.Narrative.NarrativeLineNode
  id: serena_know_line
  editorPosition: {x: 2175, y: 8045}
  character: {fileID: 0}
  emotion: {fileID: 0}
  portraitSide: 0
  text: "Something in you just can't let her go, and moreover, makes you loosen your
    grip just a little, to not hurt her. You see her looking at you. Something in
    that gaze catches you off guard. Real exhaustion. Like a someone carrying a title
    they were never meant for.\n\n<color=#FF675E>\u201CThere\u2019s nothing fair
    about this,\u201D</color> she says quietly. <color=#FF675E>\u201CNot for you.
    Not for me. Not for what they...\u201D</color> Her eyes look down for a second
    and then back at you. <color=#FF675E>\u201CThe Gods set things in motion long
    before either of us had the chance to choose.\u201D</color><color=#a674e8><i>\u201COh,
    those Gods!\u201D</i></color> Eris says, pleased. <color=#a674e8><i>\u201CHow
    fun! Being the victim, labeling a leash.\u201D</i></color>From the edge of your
    vision, Eris leans against the wall, watching the two of you with open amusement.
    <color=#a674e8>\u201CCareful, babe,\u201D</color> she hums, tilting her head.
    <color=#a674e8>\u201CGetting a little too close there...\u201D</color>Serena
    shakes her head, as if waking from her own thoughts.\n\nSerena exhales slowly.
    <color=#FF675E>\u201CI am doing what I can,\u201D</color> she whispers, <color=#FF675E>\u201Cto
    make sure he doesn\u2019t make them suffer more than they already must... but
    they just\u2026 follow. And when they can\u2019t, he\u2026\u201D</color>\n\nShe
    cuts herself off, and for the first time, she looks away, not able to look at
    you anymore."
